add('jz', 10, 10, 'Matthew Henry', 'Juízes 10:10 — Matthew Henry: Here is, I. A humble confession which Israel make to Deus in their distress, Jdg 10:10. Now they own themselves guilty, like a malefactor upon...', 'teologico');
add('jz', 11, 1, 'Matthew Henry', 'The princes and people of Gilead we left, in the close of the foregoing chapter, consulting about the choice of a general, having come to this resolve, that whoever would undertake to lead their forces against the children of Ammon should by common consent be head over all the inhabitants of Gilead. The enterprise was difficult, and it was fit that so great an encouragement as this should be proposed to him that would undertake it. Now all agreed that Jephthah, the Gileadite, was a mighty man...', 'teologico');
add('jz', 11, 4, 'Matthew Henry', 'Juízes 11:4 — Matthew Henry: Here is, I. The distress which the children of Israel were in upon the Ammonites invasion of their country, Jdg 11:4. Probably this was the...', 'teologico');
add('jz', 11, 12, 'Matthew Henry', 'Juízes 11:12 — Matthew Henry: We have here the treaty between Jephthah, now judge of Israel, and the king of the Ammonites (who is not named), that the controversy between...', 'teologico');
add('jz', 11, 29, 'Matthew Henry', 'Juízes 11:29 — Matthew Henry: We have here Jephthah triumphing in a glorious victory, but, as an alloy to his joy, troubled and distressed by an unadvised vow.\ I. Jephthah...', 'teologico');
