add('rm', 4, 17, 'Matthew Henry', 'Romanos 4:17 — Matthew Henry: Having observed when Abraham was justified by faith, and why, for the honour of Abraham and for example to us who call him father, the...', 'teologico');
add('rm', 4, 23, 'Matthew Henry', 'Romanos 4:23 — Matthew Henry: In the close of the chapter, he applies all to us; and, having abundantly proved that Abraham was justified by faith, he here concludes that...', 'teologico');
add('rm', 5, 6, 'Matthew Henry', 'Romanos 5:6 — Matthew Henry: The apostle here describes the fountain and foundation of justification, laid in the death of o Senhor Jesus. The streams are very sweet, but, if...', 'teologico');
add('rm', 7, 1, 'Matthew Henry', 'Romanos 7:1 — Matthew Henry: Among other arguments used in the foregoing chapter to persuade us against sin, and to holiness, this was one (Rom 7:14), that we are not...', 'teologico');
add('rm', 7, 7, 'Matthew Henry', 'Romanos 7:7 — Matthew Henry: To what he had said in the former paragraph, the apostle here raises an objection, which he answers very fully: What shall we say then?...', 'teologico');
add('rm', 7, 14, 'Matthew Henry', 'Romanos 7:14 — Matthew Henry: Here is a description of the conflict between grace and corruption in the heart, between the law of Deus and the law of sin. And...', 'teologico');
add('rm', 8, 10, 'Matthew Henry', 'Romanos 8:10 — Matthew Henry: In these verses the apostle represents two more excellent benefits, which belong to true believers.\ I. Life. The happiness is not barely a negative happiness,...', 'teologico');
add('rm', 8, 17, 'Matthew Henry', 'In these words the apostle describes a fourth illustrious branch of the happiness of believers, namely, a title to the future glory. This is fitly annexed to our sonship; for as the adoption of sons entitles us to that glory, so the disposition of sons fits and prepares us for it. If children, then heirs, Rom 8:17. In earthly inheritances this rule does not hold, only the first-born are heirs; but the church is a church of first-born, for they are all heirs. Heaven is an inheritance that all ...', 'teologico');
add('rm', 8, 26, 'Matthew Henry', 'Romanos 8:26 — Matthew Henry: The apostle here suggests two privileges more to which true Christians are entitled: - \ I. The help of the Spirit in prayer. While we...', 'teologico');
add('rm', 9, 6, 'Matthew Henry', 'Romanos 9:6 — Matthew Henry: The apostle, having made his way to that which he had to say, concerning the rejection of the body of his countrymen, with a protestation...', 'teologico');
add('rm', 9, 25, 'Matthew Henry', 'Romanos 9:25 — Matthew Henry: Having explained the promise, and proved the divine sovereignty, the apostle here shows how the rejection of the Jews, and the taking in of the...', 'teologico');
